# Requests for the Customer Portal API. Open this file in Visual Studio or VS Code
# (REST Client) and select "Send request" above a request.
#
# Get a token for the API from your sign-in provider and paste it below. For example, with
# the Azure CLI signed in as a test customer:
#   az account get-access-token --scope api://<customer-portal-api-client-id>/.default --query accessToken -o tsv

@host = https://localhost:7275
@token = <paste an access token here>
# A case of the signed-in customer, and a case of another customer.
@caseId = 3f2a9c1e-5b7d-4e8a-9f10-2c3d4e5f6a7b
@otherCaseId = 9b1d4e7a-2c3f-4a5b-8d6e-7f8091a2b3c4

### Which project, API and version the host loaded, and whether it is healthy
GET {{host}}/health

### A customer reads the summary of one of their own cases: 200 OK
GET {{host}}/service/incident/{{caseId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token: 401 with UNAUTHORIZED_ACCESS
GET {{host}}/service/incident/{{caseId}}/summary

### Another customer's case: refused with NOT_YOUR_CASE
GET {{host}}/service/incident/{{otherCaseId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A case that does not exist: 404 Not Found
GET {{host}}/service/incident/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
